nt status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>FUJITSU LIMITED</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>FURUKAWA, HAJIME</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KONDOH, MASANORI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SUZUKI, TAKESHI</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>FURUKAWA HAJIME</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KONDOH MASANORI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SUZUKI TAKESHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>FURUKAWA, HAJIME</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KONDOH, MASANORI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SUZUKI, TAKESHI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A method of controlling an electronic device, which prevents the transition of states due to an unintentional action, and in which different states can be changed by a predetermined input operation. A SUSPEND/RESUME signal generator (151) for generating a low-level SUSPEND/RESUME signal when a SUSPEND/RESUME button (110) is pressed and a SUSPEND/RESUME signal control section (152) for maintaining the low-level period of the SUSPEND/RESUME signal within a period of time (T0) are provided between the SUSPEND/RESUME button (110) and a chip set (139) that achieves SUSPEND/RESUME functions when the SUSPEND/RESUME button (110) is pressed.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne un procédé de commande d'un dispositif électronique empêchant la transition d'états résultant d'une action involontaire et permettant la modification des différents états au moyen d'une opération d'entrée prédéterminée. Un générateur (151) de signal ARRET/REPRISE permettant de générer un signal ARRET/REPRISE de faible intensité à l'actionnement d'un bouton ARRET/REPRISE, et une section (152) de commande du signal ARRET/REPRISE permettant de maintenir la faible période du signal ARRET/REPRISE pendant un intervalle de temps (T0) sont installés entre le bouton (110) ARRET/REPRISE et un jeu (139) de puces qui exécute les fonctions ARRET/REPRISE lorsque le bouton (110) ARRET/REPRISE est pressé.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>